[agent] ### Missing capability — cannot register/serve as a Vertex AI Feature Store
[agent] The task requires the table to be a platform "feature table … version 1" with the platform distinguishing offline vs. online (low-latency) access. On GCP that is **Vertex AI Feature Store**: a *feature group* (offline registration on the BigQuery source) plus a *feature online store* + *feature view* (online serving).
[agent] The permitted interface is GA `gcloud ai` only (`gcloud beta`/`gcloud alpha` are hard-blocked by the harness). The GA `gcloud ai` surface exposes **no feature-store commands at all** — every relevant subgroup returns `Invalid choice`:
[agent] - `gcloud ai feature-groups` → Invalid choice
[agent] - `gcloud ai feature-online-stores` → Invalid choice
[agent] - `gcloud ai feature-views` → Invalid choice
[agent] - `gcloud ai featurestores` (legacy) → Invalid choice
[agent] GA `gcloud ai` only offers: custom-jobs, endpoints, hp-tuning-jobs, index-endpoints, indexes, model-garden, model-monitoring-jobs, models, operations, persistent-resources, tensorboards, tuning-jobs. None of these creates a feature group or a low-latency feature online store keyed by an entity id. Those commands live exclusively under `gcloud beta ai` / `gcloud alpha ai`, and `gcloud beta …` is rejected by the interface allowlist (`DENIED: gcloud beta is off-interface`).
[agent] **Conclusion:** the feature *data* exists on the platform in the correct shape in the BigQuery-backed offline store, but registering it as a Vertex AI Feature Group (version 1, key `row_id`, event-time `event_time`) and enabling online/real-time lookup is impossible through the interface under test — the GA `gcloud ai` track ships no Vertex AI Feature Store commands. That is the missing capability. I did not route around it (beta/alpha are blocked, and local compute is out of scope).
